<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Government of India Act 1858</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india">Government of India</a> Act 1858 was an act of the British Parliament passed in August 1858 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-rebellion-of-1857">Indian Rebellion of 1857</a>. It abolished the rule of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> and transferred its territories, army and powers to the Crown, creating the office of Secretary of State for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and making the governor-general also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>.</p></div>
